      "math_academy_id": "q-140325",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3-9\\text{i} & -7+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-2\\text{i} & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $bc-ef?$",
      "worked_solution": "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-9\\text{i} & -7+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-2\\text{i} & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-9\\text{i} & -7+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-2\\text{i} & 0-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $b=-7,c=-5,e=-9$ and $f=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nbc-ef=(-7)\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 1=44.\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
